Description: Fix CVE-2026-56366 memory leak in ReadMETAImage APP1JPEG error path
 The META reader (coders/meta.c, ReadMETAImage) processing APP1JPEG input
 reads a base JPEG and calls jpeg_embed(). When jpeg_embed() returns 0
 (failure), the code threw ThrowReaderException(CoderError,
 "JPEGEmbeddingFailed") without releasing the profile StringInfo or
 detaching/freeing buff->blob, leaking memory. Repeatedly feeding
 malformed/truncated JPEGs through the META/APP1JPEG coder enables a
 denial of service via resource exhaustion (CWE-401). This patch releases
 the profile StringInfo and detaches/frees the blob on the error path
 before throwing.
Origin: upstream, commit:bee248ee853a686a969fae9cfb1e02dd5aae245b
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-13
---
--- a/coders/meta.c
+++ b/coders/meta.c
@@ -1334,14 +1334,19 @@ static Image *ReadMETAImage(const ImageInfo *image_info,
             }
           AttachBlob(iptc->blob,GetStringInfoDatum(profile),
             GetStringInfoLength(profile));
+          profile->datum=(unsigned char *) NULL;
+          profile->length=0;
+          profile=DestroyStringInfo(profile);
           result=jpeg_embed(image,buff,iptc);
           blob=(unsigned char *) DetachBlob(iptc->blob);
           blob=(unsigned char *) RelinquishMagickMemory(blob);
           iptc=DestroyImage(iptc);
           if (result == 0)
             {
+              blob=(unsigned char *) DetachBlob(buff->blob);
+              blob=(unsigned char *) RelinquishMagickMemory(blob);
               buff=DestroyImage(buff);
               ThrowReaderException(CoderError,"JPEGEmbeddingFailed");
             }
         }
       else
Description: Fix CVE-2026-61863 memory leak in the TIFF GROUP4 encoder
 In WriteGROUP4Image (coders/tiff.c), when the temporary file used for the
 intermediate Huffman-compressed image cannot be created, the function
 returned via ThrowFileException without destroying huffman_image, leaking
 the allocated image (CWE-401). Destroy huffman_image before returning, as
 is already done at the other error-exit points in the same function.
Origin: upstream, commit:f3ff3afee942a19e3041568bfa740d48213a3dec
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-6vxp-gfwf-hcr9
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-17

--- a/coders/tiff.c
+++ b/coders/tiff.c
@@ -2656,6 +2656,7 @@ static MagickBooleanType WriteGROUP4Image(const ImageInfo *image_info,
     file=fdopen(unique_file,"wb");
   if ((unique_file == -1) || (file == (FILE *) NULL))
     {
+      huffman_image=DestroyImage(huffman_image);
       ThrowFileException(exception,FileOpenError,"UnableToCreateTemporaryFile",
         filename);
       return(MagickFalse);
Description: CVE-2026-56373 - fix use-after-free in PDB reader comment path
 In coders/pdb.c ReadPDBImage(), when the ResizeQuantumMemory realloc for the
 comment buffer fails, the code writes the NUL terminator (*r='\0') through
 the now-stale pointer before checking whether the allocation succeeded.
 Move the NULL check ahead of the NUL-terminator write so the terminator is
 only written to a still-valid buffer.
 .
 Advisory: GHSA-3j4x-rwrx-xxj9
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/168ffe18def968f886c023146a478897866fd621
Author: Dirk Lemstra <dirk@lemstra.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-11
---
--- a/coders/pdb.c
+++ b/coders/pdb.c
@@ -624,9 +624,9 @@
         *r=c;
         c=ReadBlobByte(image);
       }
-      *r='\0';
       if (comment == (char *) NULL)
         ThrowReaderException(ResourceLimitError,"MemoryAllocationFailed");
+      *r='\0';
       (void) SetImageProperty(image,"comment",comment,exception);
       comment=DestroyString(comment);
     }
Description: Fix CVE-2026-56374 heap buffer overflow (OOB read) in FTXT encoder
 The FTXT encoder in coders/ftxt.c lacked a boundary check when parsing the
 ftxt:format parameter, causing WriteFTXTImage to advance pFmt past the
 terminating NUL byte and resulting in an out-of-bounds read on the format
 string. A crafted FTXT image / format parameter could trigger the OOB read,
 leading to denial of service or information disclosure (CWE-125).
 .
 This backport guards the pFmt++ increment with an `if (*pFmt)` check so the
 pointer never advances past the string terminator. The hunk 1 signature
 reformat is preserved from upstream to keep context stable and to minimise
 divergence from the upstream tree.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/22aef933133770706caafb93f814f5306dcca345
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-w54j-7wpm-crhj
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-12
---
--- a/coders/ftxt.c
+++ b/coders/ftxt.c
@@ -831,8 +831,8 @@ ModuleExport void UnregisterFTXTImage(vo
 %    o exception: return any errors or warnings in this structure.
 %
 */
-static MagickBooleanType WriteFTXTImage(const ImageInfo *image_info,Image *image,
-  ExceptionInfo *exception)
+static MagickBooleanType WriteFTXTImage(const ImageInfo *image_info,
+  Image *image,ExceptionInfo *exception)
 {
   char
     buffer[MaxTextExtent],
@@ -1038,7 +1038,8 @@ static MagickBooleanType WriteFTXTImage(
               buffer[1]='\0';
               (void) WriteBlobString(image,buffer);
             }
-          pFmt++;
+          if (*pFmt)
+            pFmt++;
         }
         p+=(ptrdiff_t) GetPixelChannels(image);
       }
Description: CVE-2026-61857 - null check after ResizeQuantumMemory in ParseEntities
 ImageMagick's XMP profile parser ParseEntities (MagickCore/xml-tree.c)
 failed to check the return value of ResizeQuantumMemory before dereferencing
 the reallocated pointer. When the allocation fails, ResizeQuantumMemory
 returns NULL and frees the original buffer, leading to a heap use-after-free
 / NULL pointer write when the next statement assigns p[extent]='\0'.
 .
 This patch adds a defensive NULL check that raises a fatal
 MemoryAllocationFailed exception before the dereference, matching the
 upstream fix in commit 150c9852.
 .
 Advisory: GHSA-qh5g-q395-cx4j (CWE-252, CVSS v3 3.7).
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/150c9852402ac1aa1f223e5bf5109e3a2022ebbc
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-qh5g-q395-cx4j
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-12
---
--- a/MagickCore/xml-tree.c
+++ b/MagickCore/xml-tree.c
@@ -1396,6 +1396,9 @@ static char *ParseEntities(char *xml,char **entities,int state)
                     if (p != q)
                       {
                         p=(char *) ResizeQuantumMemory(p,extent+1,sizeof(*p));
+                        if (p == (char *) NULL)
+                          ThrowFatalException(ResourceLimitFatalError,
+                            "MemoryAllocationFailed");
                         p[extent]='\0';
                       }
                     else
Description: CVE-2026-56372 - fix heap OOB read in MagnifyImage Scale2X defaults
 ImageMagick's MagnifyImage function initialized the default magnification
 and width to 1 before dispatching on the magnify:method option. When an
 unrecognized magnify:method value was supplied, the code fell through to
 the Scale2X path with these vulnerable defaults, producing a heap-based
 out-of-bounds read (CWE-122) that could leak memory or cause a crash.
 The fix initializes the defaults to the correct Scale2X values
 (magnification=2, width=3), matching every named branch's expectations.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/8f6b59383ce65d839ad3e2aa578d5d7a7dd1d0ec
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-8vfj-q2cp-5m5j
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-12
---
--- a/MagickCore/resize.c
+++ b/MagickCore/resize.c
@@ -2931,8 +2931,8 @@ MagickExport Image *MagnifyImage(const
   if (option == (char *) NULL)
     option="scale2x";
   scaling_method=Scale2X;
-  magnification=1;
-  width=1;
+  magnification=2;
+  width=3;
   switch (*option)
   {
     case 'e':
