Description: Fix CVE-2026-61866 memory leak in WriteOneJNGImage (JNG encoder)
 The JNG encoder (WriteOneJNGImage in coders/png.c) leaks the allocated
 jpeg_image_info and jpeg_image structures when the status check after
 OpenBlob() fails, because it throws the writer exception without freeing
 them first. An attacker can trigger repeated resource exhaustion via
 crafted/malformed JNG conversions (CWE-401).
 .
 This backports the upstream fix to destroy jpeg_image_info and jpeg_image
 before throwing the ResourceLimitError exception on the failed status
 check. Only the security-relevant hunk is applied; the upstream commit's
 second hunk simplifies a blob-null-check cleanup path that does not exist
 in this 7.1.1-43 source tree.
Origin: upstream, commit:0bb3578ee087f3c4f14bbf1d8883ae456fc99092
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-16
---
--- a/coders/png.c
+++ b/coders/png.c
@@ -12705,7 +12705,11 @@
       (double) jpeg_image->rows);

   if (status == MagickFalse)
-    ThrowWriterException(ResourceLimitError,"MemoryAllocationFailed");
+    {
+      jpeg_image_info=DestroyImageInfo(jpeg_image_info);
+      jpeg_image=DestroyImage(jpeg_image);
+      ThrowWriterException(ResourceLimitError,"MemoryAllocationFailed");
+    }

   if (jng_color_type == 8 || jng_color_type == 12)
     jpeg_image_info->type=GrayscaleType;
Description: Fix CVE-2026-61858 policy bypass in APNG encoder / external delegates
 CopyDelegateFile() in coders/video.c copied the delegate output to the
 caller-supplied destination filename without consulting ImageMagick's
 security policy. A crafted image/filename could therefore write files to
 paths that a restrictive policy.xml (path domain, rights="none") is meant
 to forbid, bypassing the policy. This adds a write-rights policy check on
 the destination before the copy and threads the ExceptionInfo through so a
 PolicyError "NotAuthorized" exception is raised when the write is denied.
 .
 Backport note: the upstream commit uses the helper IsPathAuthorized() and
 the ThrowPolicyException() macro from MagickCore/policy-private.h, which are
 introduced by an unrelated same-day refactor that is not present in the
 7.1.1 branch shipped by trixie. This backport instead uses the equivalent,
 already-present old-API idiom IsRightsAuthorized(PathPolicyDomain,
 WritePolicyRights,...) + ThrowMagickException(...,PolicyError,
 "NotAuthorized",...) exactly as MagickCore/blob.c does for its own write
 policy check, so no new symbols or includes are required beyond policy.h.
Origin: upstream, commit:19c11cb0aefbd627c95c4c08c44722e660025aa1
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-v3j6-27vc-7pw2
