Description: Fix CVE-2026-61861 use-after-free in FormatMagickCaption
 A use-after-free flaw exists in FormatMagickCaption() in MagickCore/annotate.c
 when a memory allocation fails and leaves a dangling pointer to freed memory.
 After calling ReplaceSpaceWithNewline(), the local pointer 'p' is reassigned
 but 's' still referenced the previous (now stale) buffer. This patch refreshes
 's' to track the new value of 'p' so subsequent uses cannot dereference freed
 memory. Can lead to denial of service or potentially other impact.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/f89d59c5370cc48b758148cbdbea84c50511fee8
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-qvxh-prvr-85w2
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-12

--- a/MagickCore/annotate.c
+++ b/MagickCore/annotate.c
@@ -672,7 +672,10 @@ MagickExport ssize_t FormatMagickCaption(Image *image,DrawInfo *draw_info,
       {
         s=p;
         if (width > image->columns)
-          p=ReplaceSpaceWithNewline(caption,s);
+          {
+            p=ReplaceSpaceWithNewline(caption,s);
+            s=p;
+          }
       }
     for (i=0; i < (ssize_t) GetUTFOctets(p); i++)
       *q++=(*(p+i));
Description: CVE-2026-61870 - Fix memory leak in ImageMagick VIFF encoder
 In WriteVIFFImage (coders/viff.c), when the VIFF colormap allocation via
 AcquireQuantumMemory fails, the code threw MemoryAllocationFailed without
 first relinquishing the previously-allocated pixel_info virtual memory,
 leaking it (CWE-401). Release pixel_info before throwing the exception.
Origin: upstream, commit:fdbf39ba9a681e53e6025d40501ae5a2bfec300
Author: Cristy <urban-warrior@imagemagick.org>
Last-Update: 2026-07-14

--- a/coders/viff.c
+++ b/coders/viff.c
@@ -1146,7 +1146,10 @@ static MagickBooleanType WriteVIFFImage(const ImageInfo *image_info,
           viff_colormap=(unsigned char *) AcquireQuantumMemory(image->colors,
             3*sizeof(*viff_colormap));
           if (viff_colormap == (unsigned char *) NULL)
-            ThrowWriterException(ResourceLimitError,"MemoryAllocationFailed");
